  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The intensity of the light from a bulb incident on a surface is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The amplitude of the magnetic field in this light-wave is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p><p>(Given : Permittivity of vacuum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>, speed of light in vacuum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "43",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The intensity is defined as energy per unit time per unit area. Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Energy density is energy per unit volume. Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Dividing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>22</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Magnetic energy density will be half of total energy density, Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>Now energy density in magnetic field is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>rms</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>rms</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#8771;</mo><mn>43</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p>"
  }
}